[{"id":"waada-6-134-2","words":["verb:waada"],"options":[{"bs":"obećava vam se","en":"you (all) are promised"},{"bs":"i obećao sam vam","en":"and I promised you (all)"},{"bs":"obećava im","en":"he promises them"},{"bs":"obećava vam","en":"he/it promises you (all)"}],"ref":"6:134","answerWord":"تُوعَدُونَ","answerSound":"audio/64473d2cd831f1546324.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Lo! that which ye are promised will surely come to pass, and ye cannot escape.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"obećati","en":"to promise"},"passage":["إِنَّ","مَا","تُوعَدُونَ","لَءَاتٍ","وَمَآ","أَنتُم","بِمُعْجِزِينَ"],"marked":[2],"facts":{"verb":"وَعَدَ"}},{"id":"waada-5-9-0","words":["verb:waada"],"options":[{"bs":"obećao je","en":"he/it promised"},{"bs":"obećao ju je","en":"he/it promised it"},{"bs":"obećali su mu","en":"they promised him"},{"bs":"obećavamo im","en":"we promise them"}],"ref":"5:9","answerWord":"وَعَدَ","answerSound":"audio/38c2c8e945c13ad97f6f.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Allah hath promised those who believe and do good works: Theirs will be forgiveness and immense reward.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"obećati","en":"to promise"},"passage":["وَعَدَ","ٱللَّهُ","ٱلَّذِينَ","ءَامَنُوا۟","وَعَمِلُوا۟","ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ","لَهُم","مَّغْفِرَةٌ","وَأَجْرٌ","عَظِيمٌ"],"marked":[0],"facts":{"verb":"وَعَدَ"}},{"id":"waada-19-75-13","words":["verb:waada"],"options":[{"bs":"obećava im se","en":"they are promised"},{"bs":"obećao vam je","en":"he/it promised you (all)"},{"bs":"i obećao sam vam","en":"and I promised you (all)"},{"bs":"zar vam obećava?","en":"does he/it promise you (all)?"}],"ref":"19:75","answerWord":"يُوعَدُونَ","answerSound":"audio/3bd323416e115bd35f8b.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Say: As for him who is in error, the Beneficent will verily prolong his span of life until, when they behold that which they were promised, whether it be punishment (in the world), or the Hour (of doom), they will know who is worse in position and who is weaker as an army.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"obećati","en":"to promise"},"passage":["قُلْ","مَن","كَانَ","فِى","ٱلضَّلَٰلَةِ","فَلْيَمْدُدْ","لَهُ","ٱلرَّحْمَٰنُ","مَدًّا","حَتَّىٰٓ","إِذَا","رَأَوْا۟","مَا","يُوعَدُونَ","إِمَّا","ٱلْعَذَابَ","وَإِمَّا","ٱلسَّاعَةَ","فَسَيَعْلَمُونَ","مَنْ","هُوَ","شَرٌّ","مَّكَانًا","وَأَضْعَفُ","جُندًا"],"marked":[13],"facts":{"verb":"وَعَدَ"}},{"id":"waada-23-95-5","words":["verb:waada"],"options":[{"bs":"obećavamo im","en":"we promise them"},{"bs":"obećao ju je","en":"he/it promised it"},{"bs":"obećano je","en":"it was promised"},{"bs":"obećao vam je","en":"he/it promised you (all)"}],"ref":"23:95","answerWord":"نَعِدُهُمْ","answerSound":"audio/900996fe43dec5d3f66f.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And verily We are Able to show thee that which We have promised them.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"obećati","en":"to promise"},"passage":["وَإِنَّا","عَلَىٰٓ","أَن","نُّرِيَكَ","مَا","نَعِدُهُمْ","لَقَٰدِرُونَ"],"marked":[5],"facts":{"verb":"وَعَدَ"}},{"id":"waada-7-44-9","words":["verb:waada"],"options":[{"bs":"obećao nam je","en":"he/it promised us"},{"bs":"obećava im se","en":"they are promised"},{"bs":"obećali smo im","en":"We have promised them"},{"bs":"obećano nam je","en":"we were promised"}],"ref":"7:44","answerWord":"وَعَدَنَا","answerSound":"audio/10be81174fd22a8f21a7.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And the dwellers of the Garden cry unto the dwellers of the Fire: We have found that which our Lord promised us (to be) the Truth. Have ye (too) found that which your Lord promised the Truth? They say: Yea, verily. And a crier in between them crieth: The curse of Allah is on evil-doers,","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"obećati","en":"to promise"},"passage":["وَنَادَىٰٓ","أَصْحَٰبُ","ٱلْجَنَّةِ","أَصْحَٰبَ","ٱلنَّارِ","أَن","قَدْ","وَجَدْنَا","مَا","وَعَدَنَا","رَبُّنَا","حَقًّا","فَهَلْ","وَجَدتُّم","مَّا","وَعَدَ","رَبُّكُمْ","حَقًّا","قَالُوا۟","نَعَمْ","فَأَذَّنَ","مُؤَذِّنٌۢ","بَيْنَهُمْ","أَن","لَّعْنَةُ","ٱللَّهِ","عَلَى","ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ"],"marked":[9],"facts":{"verb":"وَعَدَ"}},{"id":"waada-13-35-3","words":["verb:waada"],"options":[{"bs":"obećano je","en":"it was promised"},{"bs":"obećao ga je","en":"he/it promised it"},{"bs":"obećavamo im","en":"we promise them"},{"bs":"obećava","en":"he/it promises"}],"ref":"13:35","answerWord":"وُعِدَ","answerSound":"audio/54affeb4587363c09f3a.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"A similitude of the Garden which is promised unto those who keep their duty (to Allah): Underneath it rivers flow; its food is everlasting, and its shade; this is the reward of those who keep their duty, while the reward of disbelievers is the Fire.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"obećati","en":"to promise"},"passage":["مَّثَلُ","ٱلْجَنَّةِ","ٱلَّتِى","وُعِدَ","ٱلْمُتَّقُونَ","تَجْرِى","مِن","تَحْتِهَا","ٱلْأَنْهَٰرُ","أُكُلُهَا","دَآئِمٌ","وَظِلُّهَا","تِلْكَ","عُقْبَى","ٱلَّذِينَ","ٱتَّقَوا۟","وَّعُقْبَى","ٱلْكَٰفِرِينَ","ٱلنَّارُ"],"marked":[3],"facts":{"verb":"وَعَدَ"}},{"id":"waada-2-268-1","words":["verb:waada"],"options":[{"bs":"obećava vam","en":"he/it promises you (all)"},{"bs":"obećao si im","en":"you promised them"},{"bs":"obećao vam je","en":"he/it promised you (all)"},{"bs":"obećali su mu","en":"they promised him"}],"ref":"2:268","answerWord":"يَعِدُكُمُ","answerSound":"audio/744d1a930a97c392365f.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"The devil promiseth you destitution and enjoineth on you lewdness. But Allah promiseth you forgiveness from Himself with bounty. Allah is All-Embracing, All-knowing.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"obećati","en":"to promise"},"passage":["ٱلشَّيْطَٰنُ","يَعِدُكُمُ","ٱلْفَقْرَ","وَيَأْمُرُكُم","بِٱلْفَحْشَآءِ","وَٱللَّهُ","يَعِدُكُم","مَّغْفِرَةً","مِّنْهُ","وَفَضْلًا","وَٱللَّهُ","وَٰسِعٌ","عَلِيمٌ"],"marked":[1],"facts":{"verb":"وَعَدَ"}},{"id":"waada-4-120-3","words":["verb:waada"],"options":[{"bs":"obećava im","en":"promises them"},{"bs":"obećava vam se","en":"you (all) are promised"},{"bs":"obećava im se","en":"they are promised"},{"bs":"obećao je","en":"he/it promised"}],"ref":"4:120","answerWord":"يَعِدُهُمُ","answerSound":"audio/a63b868f8ba8871d6563.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"He promiseth them and stirreth up desires in them, and Satan promiseth them only to beguile.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"obećati","en":"to promise"},"passage":["يَعِدُهُمْ","وَيُمَنِّيهِمْ","وَمَا","يَعِدُهُمُ","ٱلشَّيْطَٰنُ","إِلَّا","غُرُورًا"],"marked":[3],"facts":{"verb":"وَعَدَ"}},{"id":"waada-23-83-1","words":["verb:waada"],"options":[{"bs":"obećano nam je","en":"we were promised"},{"bs":"obećava vam","en":"he/it promises you (all)"},{"bs":"obećavamo im","en":"we promise them"},{"bs":"obećao ju je","en":"he/it promised it"}],"ref":"23:83","answerWord":"وُعِدْنَا","answerSound":"audio/1ae2eec44c2aa0844381.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"We were already promised this, we and our forefathers. Lo! this is naught but fables of the men of old.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"obećati","en":"to promise"},"passage":["لَقَدْ","وُعِدْنَا","نَحْنُ","وَءَابَآؤُنَا","هَٰذَا","مِن","قَبْلُ","إِنْ","هَٰذَآ","إِلَّآ","أَسَٰطِيرُ","ٱلْأَوَّلِينَ"],"marked":[1],"facts":{"verb":"وَعَدَ"}},{"id":"waada-2-268-6","words":["verb:waada"],"options":[{"bs":"obećava vam","en":"he/it promises you (all)"},{"bs":"obećao ga je","en":"he/it promised it"},{"bs":"obećao vam je","en":"he/it promised you (all)"},{"bs":"obećao je","en":"he/it promised"}],"ref":"2:268","answerWord":"يَعِدُكُم","answerSound":"audio/f7230967d9bf394888ae.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"The devil promiseth you destitution and enjoineth on you lewdness. But Allah promiseth you forgiveness from Himself with bounty. Allah is All-Embracing, All-knowing.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"obećati","en":"to promise"},"passage":["ٱلشَّيْطَٰنُ","يَعِدُكُمُ","ٱلْفَقْرَ","وَيَأْمُرُكُم","بِٱلْفَحْشَآءِ","وَٱللَّهُ","يَعِدُكُم","مَّغْفِرَةً","مِّنْهُ","وَفَضْلًا","وَٱللَّهُ","وَٰسِعٌ","عَلِيمٌ"],"marked":[6],"facts":{"verb":"وَعَدَ"}},{"id":"waada-3-194-3","words":["verb:waada"],"options":[{"bs":"obećao si nam","en":"you promised us"},{"bs":"obećava vam","en":"he/it promises you (all)"},{"bs":"obećao vam je","en":"he/it promised you (all)"},{"bs":"obećali smo im","en":"We have promised them"}],"ref":"3:194","answerWord":"وَعَدتَّنَا","answerSound":"audio/9f87dc50a9380acbcca6.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Our Lord! And give us that which Thou hast promised to us by Thy messengers. Confound us not upon the Day of Resurrection. Lo! Thou breakest not the tryst.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"obećati","en":"to promise"},"passage":["رَبَّنَا","وَءَاتِنَا","مَا","وَعَدتَّنَا","عَلَىٰ","رُسُلِكَ","وَلَا","تُخْزِنَا","يَوْمَ","ٱلْقِيَٰمَةِ","إِنَّكَ","لَا","تُخْلِفُ","ٱلْمِيعَادَ"],"marked":[3],"facts":{"verb":"وَعَدَ"}},{"id":"waada-4-120-0","words":["verb:waada"],"options":[{"bs":"obećava im","en":"he promises them"},{"bs":"obećao vam je","en":"he/it promised you (all)"},{"bs":"obećava vam","en":"he/it promises you (all)"},{"bs":"i obećaj im!","en":"and promise them!"}],"ref":"4:120","answerWord":"يَعِدُهُمْ","answerSound":"audio/95e5aa16c4ce0fafae9b.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"He promiseth them and stirreth up desires in them, and Satan promiseth them only to beguile.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"obećati","en":"to promise"},"passage":["يَعِدُهُمْ","وَيُمَنِّيهِمْ","وَمَا","يَعِدُهُمُ","ٱلشَّيْطَٰنُ","إِلَّا","غُرُورًا"],"marked":[0],"facts":{"verb":"وَعَدَ"}},{"id":"waada-9-77-11","words":["verb:waada"],"options":[{"bs":"obećali su mu","en":"they promised him"},{"bs":"obećao nam je","en":"he/it promised us"},{"bs":"obećao ju je","en":"he/it promised it"},{"bs":"obećava vam","en":"he/it promises you (all)"}],"ref":"9:77","answerWord":"وَعَدُوهُ","answerSound":"audio/e3894d1c06880ceec91b.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"So He hath made the consequence (to be) hypocrisy in their hearts until the day when they shall meet Him, because they broke their word to Allah that they promised Him, and because they lied.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"obećati","en":"to promise"},"passage":["فَأَعْقَبَهُمْ","نِفَاقًا","فِى","قُلُوبِهِمْ","إِلَىٰ","يَوْمِ","يَلْقَوْنَهُۥ","بِمَآ","أَخْلَفُوا۟","ٱللَّهَ","مَا","وَعَدُوهُ","وَبِمَا","كَانُوا۟","يَكْذِبُونَ"],"marked":[11],"facts":{"verb":"وَعَدَ"}},{"id":"waada-9-114-8","words":["verb:waada"],"options":[{"bs":"obećao ga je","en":"he/it promised it"},{"bs":"obećao vam je","en":"he/it promised you (all)"},{"bs":"zar vam obećava?","en":"does he/it promise you (all)?"},{"bs":"obećavamo im","en":"we promise them"}],"ref":"9:114","answerWord":"وَعَدَهَآ","answerSound":"audio/f2d432698ac174b0553c.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"The prayer of Abraham for the forgiveness of his father was only because of a promise he had promised him, but when it had become clear unto him that he (his father) was an enemy to Allah he (Abraham) disowned him. Lo! Abraham was soft of heart, long-suffering.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"obećati","en":"to promise"},"passage":["وَمَا","كَانَ","ٱسْتِغْفَارُ","إِبْرَٰهِيمَ","لِأَبِيهِ","إِلَّا","عَن","مَّوْعِدَةٍ","وَعَدَهَآ","إِيَّاهُ","فَلَمَّا","تَبَيَّنَ","لَهُۥٓ","أَنَّهُۥ","عَدُوٌّ","لِّلَّهِ","تَبَرَّأَ","مِنْهُ","إِنَّ","إِبْرَٰهِيمَ","لَأَوَّٰهٌ","حَلِيمٌ"],"marked":[8],"facts":{"verb":"وَعَدَ"}},{"id":"waada-17-64-13","words":["verb:waada"],"options":[{"bs":"i obećaj im!","en":"and promise them!"},{"bs":"obećano nam je","en":"we were promised"},{"bs":"obećava im se","en":"they are promised"},{"bs":"obećao si im","en":"you promised them"}],"ref":"17:64","answerWord":"وَعِدْهُمْ","answerSound":"audio/d2d4c78d1d514bf361d0.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And excite any of them whom thou canst with thy voice, and urge thy horse and foot against them, and be a partner in their wealth and children, and promise them. Satan promiseth them only to deceive.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"obećati","en":"to promise"},"passage":["وَٱسْتَفْزِزْ","مَنِ","ٱسْتَطَعْتَ","مِنْهُم","بِصَوْتِكَ","وَأَجْلِبْ","عَلَيْهِم","بِخَيْلِكَ","وَرَجِلِكَ","وَشَارِكْهُمْ","فِى","ٱلْأَمْوَٰلِ","وَٱلْأَوْلَٰدِ","وَعِدْهُمْ","وَمَا","يَعِدُهُمُ","ٱلشَّيْطَٰنُ","إِلَّا","غُرُورًا"],"marked":[13],"facts":{"verb":"وَعَدَ"}},{"id":"waada-20-86-9","words":["verb:waada"],"options":[{"bs":"obećava vam","en":"he/it promises you (all)"},{"bs":"i obećaj im!","en":"and promise them!"},{"bs":"obećali su mu","en":"they promised him"},{"bs":"obećava","en":"he/it promises"}],"ref":"20:86","answerWord":"يَعِدْكُمْ","answerSound":"audio/7378a922c29fe70f653f.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Then Moses went back unto his folk, angry and sad. He said: O my people! Hath not your Lord promised you a fair promise? Did the time appointed then appear too long for you, or did ye wish that wrath from your Lord should come upon you, that ye broke tryst with me?","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"obećati","en":"to promise"},"passage":["فَرَجَعَ","مُوسَىٰٓ","إِلَىٰ","قَوْمِهِۦ","غَضْبَٰنَ","أَسِفًا","قَالَ","يَٰقَوْمِ","أَلَمْ","يَعِدْكُمْ","رَبُّكُمْ","وَعْدًا","حَسَنًا","أَفَطَالَ","عَلَيْكُمُ","ٱلْعَهْدُ","أَمْ","أَرَدتُّمْ","أَن","يَحِلَّ","عَلَيْكُمْ","غَضَبٌ","مِّن","رَّبِّكُمْ","فَأَخْلَفْتُم","مَّوْعِدِى"],"marked":[9],"facts":{"verb":"وَعَدَ"}},{"id":"waada-22-72-23","words":["verb:waada"],"options":[{"bs":"obećao ju je","en":"he/it promised it"},{"bs":"obećao vam je","en":"he/it promised you (all)"},{"bs":"obećano nam je","en":"we were promised"},{"bs":"obećava vam","en":"he/it promises you (all)"}],"ref":"22:72","answerWord":"وَعَدَهَا","answerSound":"audio/639ac9b491897f4611c4.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And when Our revelations are recited unto them, thou knowest the denial in the faces of those who disbelieve; they all but attack those who recite Our revelations unto them. Say: Shall I proclaim unto you worse than that? The Fire! Allah hath promised it for those who disbelieve. A hapless journey's end!","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"obećati","en":"to promise"},"passage":["وَإِذَا","تُتْلَىٰ","عَلَيْهِمْ","ءَايَٰتُنَا","بَيِّنَٰتٍ","تَعْرِفُ","فِى","وُجُوهِ","ٱلَّذِينَ","كَفَرُوا۟","ٱلْمُنكَرَ","يَكَادُونَ","يَسْطُونَ","بِٱلَّذِينَ","يَتْلُونَ","عَلَيْهِمْ","ءَايَٰتِنَا","قُلْ","أَفَأُنَبِّئُكُم","بِشَرٍّ","مِّن","ذَٰلِكُمُ","ٱلنَّارُ","وَعَدَهَا","ٱللَّهُ","ٱلَّذِينَ","كَفَرُوا۟","وَبِئْسَ","ٱلْمَصِيرُ"],"marked":[23],"facts":{"verb":"وَعَدَ"}},{"id":"waada-23-35-0","words":["verb:waada"],"options":[{"bs":"zar vam obećava?","en":"does he/it promise you (all)?"},{"bs":"obećao vam je","en":"he/it promised you (all)"},{"bs":"obećava","en":"he/it promises"},{"bs":"obećao si im","en":"you promised them"}],"ref":"23:35","answerWord":"أَيَعِدُكُمْ","answerSound":"audio/4dac8eb018ba845599a9.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Doth he promise you that you, when ye are dead and have become dust and bones, will (again) be brought forth?","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"obećati","en":"to promise"},"passage":["أَيَعِدُكُمْ","أَنَّكُمْ","إِذَا","مِتُّمْ","وَكُنتُمْ","تُرَابًا","وَعِظَٰمًا","أَنَّكُم","مُّخْرَجُونَ"],"marked":[0],"facts":{"verb":"وَعَدَ"}},{"id":"waada-28-61-1","words":["verb:waada"],"options":[{"bs":"obećali smo mu","en":"we promised him"},{"bs":"obećava im","en":"promises them"},{"bs":"obećava","en":"he/it promises"},{"bs":"obećano nam je","en":"we were promised"}],"ref":"28:61","answerWord":"وَعَدْنَٰهُ","answerSound":"audio/97a5e43fa5ba0e63d84c.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Is he whom We have promised a fair promise which he will find (true) like him whom We suffer to enjoy awhile the comfort of the life of the world, then on the Day of Resurrection he will be of those arraigned?","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"obećati","en":"to promise"},"passage":["أَفَمَن","وَعَدْنَٰهُ","وَعْدًا","حَسَنًا","فَهُوَ","لَٰقِيهِ","كَمَن","مَّتَّعْنَٰهُ","مَتَٰعَ","ٱلْحَيَوٰةِ","ٱلدُّنْيَا","ثُمَّ","هُوَ","يَوْمَ","ٱلْقِيَٰمَةِ","مِنَ","ٱلْمُحْضَرِينَ"],"marked":[1],"facts":{"verb":"وَعَدَ"}},{"id":"waada-40-8-5","words":["verb:waada"],"options":[{"bs":"obećao si im","en":"you promised them"},{"bs":"obećao ga je","en":"he/it promised it"},{"bs":"obećava vam se","en":"you (all) are promised"},{"bs":"obećao vam je","en":"he/it promised you (all)"}],"ref":"40:8","answerWord":"وَعَدتَّهُمْ","answerSound":"audio/1c3f52b84626cdd4aa16.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Our Lord! And make them enter the Gardens of Eden which thou hast promised them, with such of their fathers and their wives and their descendants as do right. Lo! Thou, only Thou, art the Mighty, the Wise.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"obećati","en":"to promise"},"passage":["رَبَّنَا","وَأَدْخِلْهُمْ","جَنَّٰتِ","عَدْنٍ","ٱلَّتِى","وَعَدتَّهُمْ","وَمَن","صَلَحَ","مِنْ","ءَابَآئِهِمْ","وَأَزْوَٰجِهِمْ","وَذُرِّيَّٰتِهِمْ","إِنَّكَ","أَنتَ","ٱلْعَزِيزُ","ٱلْحَكِيمُ"],"marked":[5],"facts":{"verb":"وَعَدَ"}},{"id":"rahima-3-132-4","words":["verb:rahima"],"options":[{"bs":"bivate pomilovani","en":"you (all) are shown mercy"},{"bs":"i smiluj nam se!","en":"and have mercy on us!"},{"bs":"smilovao si mu se","en":"you had mercy on him"},{"bs":"smilovat će im se","en":"he/it will have mercy on them"}],"ref":"3:132","answerWord":"تُرْحَمُونَ","answerSound":"audio/e7ba4eb2a441cb8d469e.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And obey Allah and the messenger, that ye may find mercy.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"smilovati se","en":"to have mercy"},"passage":["وَأَطِيعُوا۟","ٱللَّهَ","وَٱلرَّسُولَ","لَعَلَّكُمْ","تُرْحَمُونَ"],"marked":[4],"facts":{"verb":"رَحِمَ"}},{"id":"rahima-44-42-2","words":["verb:rahima"],"options":[{"bs":"smilovao se","en":"He has had mercy"},{"bs":"smilovao mu se","en":"he/it had mercy on him"},{"bs":"smiluje vam se","en":"he/it has mercy on you (all)"},{"bs":"i smiluje se","en":"and He has mercy"}],"ref":"44:42","answerWord":"رَّحِمَ","answerSound":"audio/f40df72cdc6796f4cf5b.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Save him on whom Allah hath mercy. Lo! He is the Mighty, the Merciful.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"smilovati se","en":"to have mercy"},"passage":["إِلَّا","مَن","رَّحِمَ","ٱللَّهُ","إِنَّهُۥ","هُوَ","ٱلْعَزِيزُ","ٱلرَّحِيمُ"],"marked":[2],"facts":{"verb":"رَحِمَ"}},{"id":"rahima-6-16-5","words":["verb:rahima"],"options":[{"bs":"smilovao mu se","en":"he/it had mercy on him"},{"bs":"smilovao se","en":"he/it had mercy"},{"bs":"smilovat će im se","en":"he/it will have mercy on them"},{"bs":"smiluj im se!","en":"have mercy on them (two)!"}],"ref":"6:16","answerWord":"رَحِمَهُۥ","answerSound":"audio/6ddde1ada6df45ef1253.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"He from whom (such retribution) is averted on that day, (Allah) hath in truth had mercy on him. That will be the signal triumph.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"smilovati se","en":"to have mercy"},"passage":["مَّن","يُصْرَفْ","عَنْهُ","يَوْمَئِذٍ","فَقَدْ","رَحِمَهُۥ","وَذَٰلِكَ","ٱلْفَوْزُ","ٱلْمُبِينُ"],"marked":[5],"facts":{"verb":"رَحِمَ"}},{"id":"rahima-7-149-11","words":["verb:rahima"],"options":[{"bs":"smiluje nam se","en":"he/it has mercy on us"},{"bs":"smiluj im se!","en":"have mercy on them (two)!"},{"bs":"smilovao mu se","en":"he/it had mercy on him"},{"bs":"smilovao se","en":"he/it had mercy"}],"ref":"7:149","answerWord":"يَرْحَمْنَا","answerSound":"audio/1caf457086fd50d8aefb.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And when they feared the consequences thereof and saw that they had gone astray, they said: Unless our Lord have mercy on us and forgive us, we verily are of the lost.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"smilovati se","en":"to have mercy"},"passage":["وَلَمَّا","سُقِطَ","فِىٓ","أَيْدِيهِمْ","وَرَأَوْا۟","أَنَّهُمْ","قَدْ","ضَلُّوا۟","قَالُوا۟","لَئِن","لَّمْ","يَرْحَمْنَا","رَبُّنَا","وَيَغْفِرْ","لَنَا","لَنَكُونَنَّ","مِنَ","ٱلْخَٰسِرِينَ"],"marked":[11],"facts":{"verb":"رَحِمَ"}},{"id":"rahima-9-71-18","words":["verb:rahima"],"options":[{"bs":"smilovat će im se","en":"he/it will have mercy on them"},{"bs":"i smiluj se","en":"and have mercy"},{"bs":"i smiluje se","en":"and He has mercy"},{"bs":"smilovao se","en":"He has had mercy"}],"ref":"9:71","answerWord":"سَيَرْحَمُهُمُ","answerSound":"audio/d5e68f15ad017c8303f7.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And the believers, men and women, are protecting friends one of another; they enjoin the right and forbid the wrong, and they establish worship and they pay the poor-due, and they obey Allah and His messenger. As for these, Allah will have mercy on them. Lo! Allah is Mighty, Wise.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"smilovati se","en":"to have mercy"},"passage":["وَٱلْمُؤْمِنُونَ","وَٱلْمُؤْمِنَٰتُ","بَعْضُهُمْ","أَوْلِيَآءُ","بَعْضٍ","يَأْمُرُونَ","بِٱلْمَعْرُوفِ","وَيَنْهَوْنَ","عَنِ","ٱلْمُنكَرِ","وَيُقِيمُونَ","ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ","وَيُؤْتُونَ","ٱلزَّكَوٰةَ","وَيُطِيعُونَ","ٱللَّهَ","وَرَسُولَهُۥٓ","أُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ","سَيَرْحَمُهُمُ","ٱللَّهُ","إِنَّ","ٱللَّهَ","عَزِيزٌ","حَكِيمٌ"],"marked":[18],"facts":{"verb":"رَحِمَ"}},{"id":"rahima-12-53-9","words":["verb:rahima"],"options":[{"bs":"smilovao se","en":"he/it had mercy"},{"bs":"smiluje vam se","en":"he/it has mercy on you (all)"},{"bs":"smilovao mu se","en":"he/it had mercy on him"},{"bs":"smilovao nam se","en":"he/it had mercy on us"}],"ref":"12:53","answerWord":"رَحِمَ","answerSound":"audio/89ead17b7db1d025b605.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"I do not exculpate myself. Lo! the (human) soul enjoineth unto evil, save that whereon my Lord hath mercy. Lo! my Lord is Forgiving, Merciful.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"smilovati se","en":"to have mercy"},"passage":["وَمَآ","أُبَرِّئُ","نَفْسِىٓ","إِنَّ","ٱلنَّفْسَ","لَأَمَّارَةٌۢ","بِٱلسُّوٓءِ","إِلَّا","مَا","رَحِمَ","رَبِّىٓ","إِنَّ","رَبِّى","غَفُورٌ","رَّحِيمٌ"],"marked":[9],"facts":{"verb":"رَحِمَ"}},{"id":"rahima-17-8-3","words":["verb:rahima"],"options":[{"bs":"smiluje vam se","en":"he/it has mercy on you (all)"},{"bs":"i smiluj nam se!","en":"and have mercy on us!"},{"bs":"bivate pomilovani","en":"you (all) are shown mercy"},{"bs":"smilovao se","en":"he/it had mercy"}],"ref":"17:8","answerWord":"يَرْحَمَكُمْ","answerSound":"audio/6fc0744f2933772f867d.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"It may be that your Lord will have mercy on you, but if ye repeat (the crime) We shall repeat (the punishment), and We have appointed hell a dungeon for the disbelievers.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"smilovati se","en":"to have mercy"},"passage":["عَسَىٰ","رَبُّكُمْ","أَن","يَرْحَمَكُمْ","وَإِنْ","عُدتُّمْ","عُدْنَا","وَجَعَلْنَا","جَهَنَّمَ","لِلْكَٰفِرِينَ","حَصِيرًا"],"marked":[3],"facts":{"verb":"رَحِمَ"}},{"id":"rahima-17-24-8","words":["verb:rahima"],"options":[{"bs":"smiluj im se!","en":"have mercy on them (two)!"},{"bs":"smiluje vam se","en":"he/it has mercy on you (all)"},{"bs":"bivate pomilovani","en":"you (all) are shown mercy"},{"bs":"smilovao se","en":"he/it had mercy"}],"ref":"17:24","answerWord":"ٱرْحَمْهُمَا","answerSound":"audio/696dce3fe3df9dc2abc2.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And lower unto them the wing of submission through mercy, and say: My Lord! Have mercy on them both as they did care for me when I was little.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"smilovati se","en":"to have mercy"},"passage":["وَٱخْفِضْ","لَهُمَا","جَنَاحَ","ٱلذُّلِّ","مِنَ","ٱلرَّحْمَةِ","وَقُل","رَّبِّ","ٱرْحَمْهُمَا","كَمَا","رَبَّيَانِى","صَغِيرًا"],"marked":[8],"facts":{"verb":"رَحِمَ"}},{"id":"rahima-17-54-5","words":["verb:rahima"],"options":[{"bs":"smiluje vam se","en":"he/it has mercy on you (all)"},{"bs":"i smiluje se","en":"and He has mercy"},{"bs":"i smiluj se","en":"and have mercy"},{"bs":"bivate pomilovani","en":"you (all) are shown mercy"}],"ref":"17:54","answerWord":"يَرْحَمْكُمْ","answerSound":"audio/b95e6237a9b9056d3355.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Your Lord is Best Aware of you. If He will, He will have mercy on you, or if He will, He will punish you. We have not sent thee (O Muhammad) as a warden over them.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"smilovati se","en":"to have mercy"},"passage":["رَّبُّكُمْ","أَعْلَمُ","بِكُمْ","إِن","يَشَأْ","يَرْحَمْكُمْ","أَوْ","إِن","يَشَأْ","يُعَذِّبْكُمْ","وَمَآ","أَرْسَلْنَٰكَ","عَلَيْهِمْ","وَكِيلًا"],"marked":[5],"facts":{"verb":"رَحِمَ"}},{"id":"rahima-23-75-1","words":["verb:rahima"],"options":[{"bs":"smilovali smo im se","en":"we had mercy on them"},{"bs":"smilovao mu se","en":"he/it had mercy on him"},{"bs":"i smiluje se","en":"and He has mercy"},{"bs":"smilovao se","en":"he/it had mercy"}],"ref":"23:75","answerWord":"رَحِمْنَٰهُمْ","answerSound":"audio/8e54c8364a5b5f67a4de.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Though We had mercy on them and relieved them of the harm afflicting them, they still would wander blindly on in their contumacy.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"smilovati se","en":"to have mercy"},"passage":["وَلَوْ","رَحِمْنَٰهُمْ","وَكَشَفْنَا","مَا","بِهِم","مِّن","ضُرٍّ","لَّلَجُّوا۟","فِى","طُغْيَٰنِهِمْ","يَعْمَهُونَ"],"marked":[1],"facts":{"verb":"رَحِمَ"}},{"id":"rahima-23-118-3","words":["verb:rahima"],"options":[{"bs":"i smiluj se","en":"and have mercy"},{"bs":"smilovao nam se","en":"he/it had mercy on us"},{"bs":"smiluje vam se","en":"he/it has mercy on you (all)"},{"bs":"smiluj im se!","en":"have mercy on them (two)!"}],"ref":"23:118","answerWord":"وَٱرْحَمْ","answerSound":"audio/93227c1806515549b320.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And (O Muhammad) say: My Lord! Forgive and have mercy, for Thou art Best of all who show mercy.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"smilovati se","en":"to have mercy"},"passage":["وَقُل","رَّبِّ","ٱغْفِرْ","وَٱرْحَمْ","وَأَنتَ","خَيْرُ","ٱلرَّٰحِمِينَ"],"marked":[3],"facts":{"verb":"رَحِمَ"}},{"id":"rahima-29-21-3","words":["verb:rahima"],"options":[{"bs":"i smiluje se","en":"and He has mercy"},{"bs":"i smiluj nam se!","en":"and have mercy on us!"},{"bs":"smilovao se","en":"He has had mercy"},{"bs":"i smiluj se","en":"and have mercy"}],"ref":"29:21","answerWord":"وَيَرْحَمُ","answerSound":"audio/42135e2252049fe6a6b4.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"He punisheth whom He will and showeth mercy unto whom He will, and unto Him ye will be turned.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"smilovati se","en":"to have mercy"},"passage":["يُعَذِّبُ","مَن","يَشَآءُ","وَيَرْحَمُ","مَن","يَشَآءُ","وَإِلَيْهِ","تُقْلَبُونَ"],"marked":[3],"facts":{"verb":"رَحِمَ"}},{"id":"rahima-40-9-7","words":["verb:rahima"],"options":[{"bs":"smilovao si mu se","en":"you had mercy on him"},{"bs":"smiluje nam se","en":"he/it has mercy on us"},{"bs":"smiluje vam se","en":"he/it has mercy on you (all)"},{"bs":"i smiluje se","en":"and He has mercy"}],"ref":"40:9","answerWord":"رَحِمْتَهُۥ","answerSound":"audio/68b9724f493925619a2a.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And ward off from them ill-deeds; and he from whom Thou wardest off ill-deeds that day, him verily hast Thou taken into mercy. That is the supreme triumph.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"smilovati se","en":"to have mercy"},"passage":["وَقِهِمُ","ٱلسَّيِّـَٔاتِ","وَمَن","تَقِ","ٱلسَّيِّـَٔاتِ","يَوْمَئِذٍ","فَقَدْ","رَحِمْتَهُۥ","وَذَٰلِكَ","هُوَ","ٱلْفَوْزُ","ٱلْعَظِيمُ"],"marked":[7],"facts":{"verb":"رَحِمَ"}},{"id":"rahima-67-28-8","words":["verb:rahima"],"options":[{"bs":"smilovao nam se","en":"he/it had mercy on us"},{"bs":"smilovali smo im se","en":"we had mercy on them"},{"bs":"i smiluj nam se!","en":"and have mercy on us!"},{"bs":"smilovao si mu se","en":"you had mercy on him"}],"ref":"67:28","answerWord":"رَحِمَنَا","answerSound":"audio/e1d0c1134ca76469f5f5.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Say (O Muhammad): Have ye thought: Whether Allah causeth me (Muhammad) and those with me to perish or hath mercy on us, still, who will protect the disbelievers from a painful doom?","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"smilovati se","en":"to have mercy"},"passage":["قُلْ","أَرَءَيْتُمْ","إِنْ","أَهْلَكَنِىَ","ٱللَّهُ","وَمَن","مَّعِىَ","أَوْ","رَحِمَنَا","فَمَن","يُجِيرُ","ٱلْكَٰفِرِينَ","مِنْ","عَذَابٍ","أَلِيمٍ"],"marked":[8],"facts":{"verb":"رَحِمَ"}},{"id":"masha-67-22-1","words":["verb:masha"],"options":[{"bs":"hoda","en":"he/it walks"},{"bs":"hodaju","en":"they walk"},{"bs":"pa hodajte!","en":"so (you all) walk!"},{"bs":"hodali su","en":"they walked"}],"ref":"67:22","answerWord":"يَمْشِى","answerSound":"audio/58cc2c2ae9e2e90b4c52.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Is he who goeth groping on his face more rightly guided, or he who walketh upright on a straight road?","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"hodati","en":"to walk"},"passage":["أَفَمَن","يَمْشِى","مُكِبًّا","عَلَىٰ","وَجْهِهِۦٓ","أَهْدَىٰٓ","أَمَّن","يَمْشِى","سَوِيًّا","عَلَىٰ","صِرَٰطٍ","مُّسْتَقِيمٍ"],"marked":[1,7],"facts":{"verb":"مَشَى"}},{"id":"masha-25-63-3","words":["verb:masha"],"options":[{"bs":"hodaju","en":"they walk"},{"bs":"hoda","en":"he/it walks"},{"bs":"idite","en":"walk on"},{"bs":"hodali su","en":"they walked"}],"ref":"25:63","answerWord":"يَمْشُونَ","answerSound":"audio/72c37d6f86b73459b32f.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"The (faithful) slaves of the Beneficent are they who walk upon the earth modestly, and when the foolish ones address them answer: Peace;","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"hodati","en":"to walk"},"passage":["وَعِبَادُ","ٱلرَّحْمَٰنِ","ٱلَّذِينَ","يَمْشُونَ","عَلَى","ٱلْأَرْضِ","هَوْنًا","وَإِذَا","خَاطَبَهُمُ","ٱلْجَٰهِلُونَ","قَالُوا۟","سَلَٰمًا"],"marked":[3],"facts":{"verb":"مَشَى"}},{"id":"masha-2-20-7","words":["verb:masha"],"options":[{"bs":"hodali su","en":"they walked"},{"bs":"i hoda","en":"and he/it walks"},{"bs":"idite","en":"walk on"},{"bs":"i hodaju","en":"and they walk"}],"ref":"2:20","answerWord":"مَّشَوْا۟","answerSound":"audio/8d94dce04e60339a9911.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"The lightning almost snatcheth away their sight from them. As often as it flasheth forth for them they walk therein, and when it darkeneth against them they stand still. If Allah willed, He could destroy their hearing and their sight. Lo! Allah is able to do all things.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"hodati","en":"to walk"},"passage":["يَكَادُ","ٱلْبَرْقُ","يَخْطَفُ","أَبْصَٰرَهُمْ","كُلَّمَآ","أَضَآءَ","لَهُم","مَّشَوْا۟","فِيهِ","وَإِذَآ","أَظْلَمَ","عَلَيْهِمْ","قَامُوا۟","وَلَوْ","شَآءَ","ٱللَّهُ","لَذَهَبَ","بِسَمْعِهِمْ","وَأَبْصَٰرِهِمْ","إِنَّ","ٱللَّهَ","عَلَىٰ","كُلِّ","شَىْءٍ","قَدِيرٌ"],"marked":[7],"facts":{"verb":"مَشَى"}},{"id":"masha-25-7-6","words":["verb:masha"],"options":[{"bs":"i hoda","en":"and he/it walks"},{"bs":"hodate","en":"you (all) walk"},{"bs":"idite","en":"walk on"},{"bs":"hodaju","en":"they walk"}],"ref":"25:7","answerWord":"وَيَمْشِى","answerSound":"audio/e382f4473f5bf04b9572.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And they say: What aileth this messenger (of Allah) that he eateth food and walketh in the markets? Why is not an angel sent down unto him, to be a warner with him.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"hodati","en":"to walk"},"passage":["وَقَالُوا۟","مَالِ","هَٰذَا","ٱلرَّسُولِ","يَأْكُلُ","ٱلطَّعَامَ","وَيَمْشِى","فِى","ٱلْأَسْوَاقِ","لَوْلَآ","أُنزِلَ","إِلَيْهِ","مَلَكٌ","فَيَكُونَ","مَعَهُۥ","نَذِيرًا"],"marked":[6],"facts":{"verb":"مَشَى"}},{"id":"masha-25-20-9","words":["verb:masha"],"options":[{"bs":"i hodaju","en":"and they walk"},{"bs":"idite","en":"walk on"},{"bs":"i hoda","en":"and he/it walks"},{"bs":"hodali su","en":"they walked"}],"ref":"25:20","answerWord":"وَيَمْشُونَ","answerSound":"audio/85cf8275fd6af812c5f7.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"We never sent before thee any messengers but lo! they verily ate food and walked in the markets. And We have appointed some of you a test for others: Will ye be steadfast? And thy Lord is ever Seer.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"hodati","en":"to walk"},"passage":["وَمَآ","أَرْسَلْنَا","قَبْلَكَ","مِنَ","ٱلْمُرْسَلِينَ","إِلَّآ","إِنَّهُمْ","لَيَأْكُلُونَ","ٱلطَّعَامَ","وَيَمْشُونَ","فِى","ٱلْأَسْوَاقِ","وَجَعَلْنَا","بَعْضَكُمْ","لِبَعْضٍ","فِتْنَةً","أَتَصْبِرُونَ","وَكَانَ","رَبُّكَ","بَصِيرًا"],"marked":[9],"facts":{"verb":"مَشَى"}},{"id":"masha-38-6-4","words":["verb:masha"],"options":[{"bs":"idite","en":"walk on"},{"bs":"i hodaju","en":"and they walk"},{"bs":"i hoda","en":"and he/it walks"},{"bs":"hodali su","en":"they walked"}],"ref":"38:6","answerWord":"ٱمْشُوا۟","answerSound":"audio/4e21b5211b5246334b4d.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"The chiefs among them go about, exhorting: Go and be staunch to your gods! Lo! this is a thing designed.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"hodati","en":"to walk"},"passage":["وَٱنطَلَقَ","ٱلْمَلَأُ","مِنْهُمْ","أَنِ","ٱمْشُوا۟","وَٱصْبِرُوا۟","عَلَىٰٓ","ءَالِهَتِكُمْ","إِنَّ","هَٰذَا","لَشَىْءٌ","يُرَادُ"],"marked":[4],"facts":{"verb":"مَشَى"}},{"id":"masha-57-28-14","words":["verb:masha"],"options":[{"bs":"hodate","en":"you (all) walk"},{"bs":"i hoda","en":"and he/it walks"},{"bs":"pa hodajte!","en":"so (you all) walk!"},{"bs":"hodali su","en":"they walked"}],"ref":"57:28","answerWord":"تَمْشُونَ","answerSound":"audio/cfe1aa618fa6500c1822.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"O ye who believe! Be mindful of your duty to Allah and put faith in His messenger. He will give you twofold of His mercy and will appoint for you a light wherein ye shall walk, and will forgive you. Allah is Forgiving, Merciful;","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"hodati","en":"to walk"},"passage":["يَٰٓأَيُّهَا","ٱلَّذِينَ","ءَامَنُوا۟","ٱتَّقُوا۟","ٱللَّهَ","وَءَامِنُوا۟","بِرَسُولِهِۦ","يُؤْتِكُمْ","كِفْلَيْنِ","مِن","رَّحْمَتِهِۦ","وَيَجْعَل","لَّكُمْ","نُورًا","تَمْشُونَ","بِهِۦ","وَيَغْفِرْ","لَكُمْ","وَٱللَّهُ","غَفُورٌ","رَّحِيمٌ"],"marked":[14],"facts":{"verb":"مَشَى"}},{"id":"masha-67-15-6","words":["verb:masha"],"options":[{"bs":"pa hodajte!","en":"so (you all) walk!"},{"bs":"hodaju","en":"they walk"},{"bs":"i hoda","en":"and he/it walks"},{"bs":"hodali su","en":"they walked"}],"ref":"67:15","answerWord":"فَٱمْشُوا۟","answerSound":"audio/289b77c5d698ee7c64b4.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"He it is Who hath made the earth subservient unto you, so Walk in the paths thereof and eat of His providence. And unto Him will be the resurrection (of the dead).","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"hodati","en":"to walk"},"passage":["هُوَ","ٱلَّذِى","جَعَلَ","لَكُمُ","ٱلْأَرْضَ","ذَلُولًا","فَٱمْشُوا۟","فِى","مَنَاكِبِهَا","وَكُلُوا۟","مِن","رِّزْقِهِۦ","وَإِلَيْهِ","ٱلنُّشُورُ"],"marked":[6],"facts":{"verb":"مَشَى"}},{"id":"zakka-2-129-11","words":["verb:zakka"],"options":[{"bs":"i pročišćava ih","en":"and he/it purifies them"},{"bs":"pročišćavate","en":"you (all) purify"},{"bs":"i pročišćava vas","en":"and he/it purifies you (all)"},{"bs":"pročišćavaju","en":"they purify"}],"ref":"2:129","answerWord":"وَيُزَكِّيهِمْ","answerSound":"audio/86a552c6d5f2ac9144db.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Our Lord! And raise up in their midst a messenger from among them who shall recite unto them Thy revelations, and shall instruct them in the Scripture and in wisdom and shall make them grow. Lo! Thou, only Thou, art the Mighty, Wise.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"pročistiti, očistiti","en":"to purify"},"passage":["رَبَّنَا","وَٱبْعَثْ","فِيهِمْ","رَسُولًا","مِّنْهُمْ","يَتْلُوا۟","عَلَيْهِمْ","ءَايَٰتِكَ","وَيُعَلِّمُهُمُ","ٱلْكِتَٰبَ","وَٱلْحِكْمَةَ","وَيُزَكِّيهِمْ","إِنَّكَ","أَنتَ","ٱلْعَزِيزُ","ٱلْحَكِيمُ"],"marked":[11],"facts":{"verb":"زَكَّى"}},{"id":"zakka-2-174-25","words":["verb:zakka"],"options":[{"bs":"pročišćava ih","en":"he/it purifies them"},{"bs":"pročišćavaju","en":"they purify"},{"bs":"pročišćava","en":"he/it purifies"},{"bs":"pročisti je","en":"purifies it"}],"ref":"2:174","answerWord":"يُزَكِّيهِمْ","answerSound":"audio/f35cf61199caec922bbd.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Lo! those who hide aught of the Scripture which Allah hath revealed and purchase a small gain therewith, they eat into their bellies nothing else than fire. Allah will not speak to them on the Day of Resurrection, nor will He make them grow. Theirs will be a painful doom.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"pročistiti, očistiti","en":"to purify"},"passage":["إِنَّ","ٱلَّذِينَ","يَكْتُمُونَ","مَآ","أَنزَلَ","ٱللَّهُ","مِنَ","ٱلْكِتَٰبِ","وَيَشْتَرُونَ","بِهِۦ","ثَمَنًا","قَلِيلًا","أُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ","مَا","يَأْكُلُونَ","فِى","بُطُونِهِمْ","إِلَّا","ٱلنَّارَ","وَلَا","يُكَلِّمُهُمُ","ٱللَّهُ","يَوْمَ","ٱلْقِيَٰمَةِ","وَلَا","يُزَكِّيهِمْ","وَلَهُمْ","عَذَابٌ","أَلِيمٌ"],"marked":[25],"facts":{"verb":"زَكَّى"}},{"id":"zakka-4-49-8","words":["verb:zakka"],"options":[{"bs":"pročišćava","en":"he/it purifies"},{"bs":"i pročišćava ih","en":"and he/it purifies them"},{"bs":"i pročišćava vas","en":"and he/it purifies you (all)"},{"bs":"pročišćavaju","en":"they purify"}],"ref":"4:49","answerWord":"يُزَكِّى","answerSound":"audio/23b117fd0077a851f6c7.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Hast thou not seen those who praise themselves for purity? Nay, Allah purifieth whom He will, and they will not be wronged even the hair upon a date-stone.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"pročistiti, očistiti","en":"to purify"},"passage":["أَلَمْ","تَرَ","إِلَى","ٱلَّذِينَ","يُزَكُّونَ","أَنفُسَهُم","بَلِ","ٱللَّهُ","يُزَكِّى","مَن","يَشَآءُ","وَلَا","يُظْلَمُونَ","فَتِيلًا"],"marked":[8],"facts":{"verb":"زَكَّى"}},{"id":"zakka-2-151-8","words":["verb:zakka"],"options":[{"bs":"i pročišćava vas","en":"and he/it purifies you (all)"},{"bs":"pročišćavate","en":"you (all) purify"},{"bs":"pročišćava ih","en":"he/it purifies them"},{"bs":"pročišćavaju","en":"they purify"}],"ref":"2:151","answerWord":"وَيُزَكِّيكُمْ","answerSound":"audio/559959a35d8740196cf4.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Even as We have sent unto you a messenger from among you, who reciteth unto you Our revelations and causeth you to grow, and teacheth you the Scripture and wisdom, and teacheth you that which ye knew not.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"pročistiti, očistiti","en":"to purify"},"passage":["كَمَآ","أَرْسَلْنَا","فِيكُمْ","رَسُولًا","مِّنكُمْ","يَتْلُوا۟","عَلَيْكُمْ","ءَايَٰتِنَا","وَيُزَكِّيكُمْ","وَيُعَلِّمُكُمُ","ٱلْكِتَٰبَ","وَٱلْحِكْمَةَ","وَيُعَلِّمُكُم","مَّا","لَمْ","تَكُونُوا۟","تَعْلَمُونَ"],"marked":[8],"facts":{"verb":"زَكَّى"}},{"id":"zakka-4-49-4","words":["verb:zakka"],"options":[{"bs":"pročišćavaju","en":"they purify"},{"bs":"pročišćavate","en":"you (all) purify"},{"bs":"pročišćava ih","en":"he/it purifies them"},{"bs":"pročisti je","en":"purifies it"}],"ref":"4:49","answerWord":"يُزَكُّونَ","answerSound":"audio/b6f333aaeca78d0ad4a7.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Hast thou not seen those who praise themselves for purity? Nay, Allah purifieth whom He will, and they will not be wronged even the hair upon a date-stone.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"pročistiti, očistiti","en":"to purify"},"passage":["أَلَمْ","تَرَ","إِلَى","ٱلَّذِينَ","يُزَكُّونَ","أَنفُسَهُم","بَلِ","ٱللَّهُ","يُزَكِّى","مَن","يَشَآءُ","وَلَا","يُظْلَمُونَ","فَتِيلًا"],"marked":[4],"facts":{"verb":"زَكَّى"}},{"id":"zakka-91-9-3","words":["verb:zakka"],"options":[{"bs":"pročisti je","en":"purifies it"},{"bs":"pročišćava ih","en":"he/it purifies them"},{"bs":"pročišćavaju","en":"they purify"},{"bs":"i pročišćava vas","en":"and he/it purifies you (all)"}],"ref":"91:9","answerWord":"زَكَّىٰهَا","answerSound":"audio/4388ef8b37b0f7785c7c.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"He is indeed successful who causeth it to grow,","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"pročistiti, očistiti","en":"to purify"},"passage":["قَدْ","أَفْلَحَ","مَن","زَكَّىٰهَا"],"marked":[3],"facts":{"verb":"زَكَّى"}},{"id":"irtadda-5-21-9","words":["verb:irtadda"],"options":[{"bs":"vraćate se","en":"you (all) turn back"},{"bs":"(ne) vraća se","en":"(does not) return"},{"bs":"pa se vratio","en":"so he/it turned back"},{"bs":"pa su se njih dvojica vratili","en":"so they both turned back"}],"ref":"5:21","answerWord":"تَرْتَدُّوا۟","answerSound":"audio/cbb6169d823be2b8b03d.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"O my people! Go into the holy land which Allah hath ordained for you. Turn not in flight, for surely ye turn back as losers:","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"vratiti se, okrenuti se natrag","en":"to turn back, to go back"},"passage":["يَٰقَوْمِ","ٱدْخُلُوا۟","ٱلْأَرْضَ","ٱلْمُقَدَّسَةَ","ٱلَّتِى","كَتَبَ","ٱللَّهُ","لَكُمْ","وَلَا","تَرْتَدُّوا۟","عَلَىٰٓ","أَدْبَارِكُمْ","فَتَنقَلِبُوا۟","خَٰسِرِينَ"],"marked":[9],"facts":{"verb":"ارْتَدَّ"}},{"id":"irtadda-12-96-7","words":["verb:irtadda"],"options":[{"bs":"pa se vratio","en":"so he/it turned back"},{"bs":"pa su se njih dvojica vratili","en":"so they both turned back"},{"bs":"vratili su se","en":"they turned back"},{"bs":"vraćate se","en":"you (all) turn back"}],"ref":"12:96","answerWord":"فَٱرْتَدَّ","answerSound":"audio/7e6063efcb8fb6590083.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Then, when the bearer of glad tidings came, he laid it on his face and he became a seer once more. He said: Said I not unto you that I know from Allah that which ye know not?","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"vratiti se, okrenuti se natrag","en":"to turn back, to go back"},"passage":["فَلَمَّآ","أَن","جَآءَ","ٱلْبَشِيرُ","أَلْقَىٰهُ","عَلَىٰ","وَجْهِهِۦ","فَٱرْتَدَّ","بَصِيرًا","قَالَ","أَلَمْ","أَقُل","لَّكُمْ","إِنِّىٓ","أَعْلَمُ","مِنَ","ٱللَّهِ","مَا","لَا","تَعْلَمُونَ"],"marked":[7],"facts":{"verb":"ارْتَدَّ"}},{"id":"irtadda-14-43-4","words":["verb:irtadda"],"options":[{"bs":"(ne) vraća se","en":"(does not) return"},{"bs":"pa se vratio","en":"so he/it turned back"},{"bs":"vratili su se","en":"they turned back"},{"bs":"pa su se njih dvojica vratili","en":"so they both turned back"}],"ref":"14:43","answerWord":"يَرْتَدُّ","answerSound":"audio/27d4a39ae6edd30115aa.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"As they come hurrying on in fear, their heads upraised, their gaze returning not to them, and their hearts as air.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"vratiti se, okrenuti se natrag","en":"to turn back, to go back"},"passage":["مُهْطِعِينَ","مُقْنِعِى","رُءُوسِهِمْ","لَا","يَرْتَدُّ","إِلَيْهِمْ","طَرْفُهُمْ","وَأَفْـِٔدَتُهُمْ","هَوَآءٌ"],"marked":[4],"facts":{"verb":"ارْتَدَّ"}},{"id":"samma-7-71-11","words":["verb:samma"],"options":[{"bs":"nazvali ste ih","en":"you (all) named them"},{"bs":"zaista nazivaju","en":"they surely name"},{"bs":"nazovite ih!","en":"(you all) name them!"},{"bs":"nazvao vas je","en":"he/it named you (all)"}],"ref":"7:71","answerWord":"سَمَّيْتُمُوهَآ","answerSound":"audio/c0945eef4c69e243774f.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"He said: Terror and wrath from your Lord have already fallen on you. Would ye wrangle with me over names which ye have named, ye and your fathers, for which no warrant from Allah hath been revealed? Then await (the consequence), lo! I (also) am of those awaiting (it).","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"nazvati, dati ime","en":"to name"},"passage":["قَالَ","قَدْ","وَقَعَ","عَلَيْكُم","مِّن","رَّبِّكُمْ","رِجْسٌ","وَغَضَبٌ","أَتُجَٰدِلُونَنِى","فِىٓ","أَسْمَآءٍ","سَمَّيْتُمُوهَآ","أَنتُمْ","وَءَابَآؤُكُم","مَّا","نَزَّلَ","ٱللَّهُ","بِهَا","مِن","سُلْطَٰنٍ","فَٱنتَظِرُوٓا۟","إِنِّى","مَعَكُم","مِّنَ","ٱلْمُنتَظِرِينَ"],"marked":[11],"facts":{"verb":"سَمَّى"}},{"id":"samma-3-36-15","words":["verb:samma"],"options":[{"bs":"nazvao sam je","en":"I named her"},{"bs":"nazvao vas je","en":"he/it named you (all)"},{"bs":"nazvali ste ih","en":"you (all) named them"},{"bs":"zaista nazivaju","en":"they surely name"}],"ref":"3:36","answerWord":"سَمَّيْتُهَا","answerSound":"audio/07d318e1618d922b8f0f.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And when she was delivered she said: My Lord! Lo! I am delivered of a female - Allah knew best of what she was delivered - the male is not as the female; and lo! I have named her Mary, and lo! I crave Thy protection for her and for her offspring from Satan the outcast.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"nazvati, dati ime","en":"to name"},"passage":["فَلَمَّا","وَضَعَتْهَا","قَالَتْ","رَبِّ","إِنِّى","وَضَعْتُهَآ","أُنثَىٰ","وَٱللَّهُ","أَعْلَمُ","بِمَا","وَضَعَتْ","وَلَيْسَ","ٱلذَّكَرُ","كَٱلْأُنثَىٰ","وَإِنِّى","سَمَّيْتُهَا","مَرْيَمَ","وَإِنِّىٓ","أُعِيذُهَا","بِكَ","وَذُرِّيَّتَهَا","مِنَ","ٱلشَّيْطَٰنِ","ٱلرَّجِيمِ"],"marked":[15],"facts":{"verb":"سَمَّى"}},{"id":"samma-53-27-5","words":["verb:samma"],"options":[{"bs":"zaista nazivaju","en":"they surely name"},{"bs":"nazovite ih!","en":"(you all) name them!"},{"bs":"nazvao sam je","en":"I named her"},{"bs":"nazvao vas je","en":"he/it named you (all)"}],"ref":"53:27","answerWord":"لَيُسَمُّونَ","answerSound":"audio/66e326d1e6af574946ef.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Lo! it is those who disbelieve in the Hereafter who name the angels with the names of females.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"nazvati, dati ime","en":"to name"},"passage":["إِنَّ","ٱلَّذِينَ","لَا","يُؤْمِنُونَ","بِٱلْءَاخِرَةِ","لَيُسَمُّونَ","ٱلْمَلَٰٓئِكَةَ","تَسْمِيَةَ","ٱلْأُنثَىٰ"],"marked":[5],"facts":{"verb":"سَمَّى"}},{"id":"istakhlafa-6-133-7","words":["verb:istakhlafa"],"options":[{"bs":"i postavlja za nasljednika","en":"and he/it appoints as successor"},{"bs":"zaista će ih postaviti za nasljednike","en":"surely he/it will appoint them as successors"},{"bs":"i postavlja vas za nasljednike","en":"and he/it appoints you (all) as successors"},{"bs":"postavio je za nasljednika","en":"he/it appointed as successor"}],"ref":"6:133","answerWord":"وَيَسْتَخْلِفْ","answerSound":"audio/affd17ce2d759f4c6744.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"Thy Lord is the Absolute, the Lord of Mercy. If He will, He can remove you and can cause what He will to follow after you, even as He raised you from the seed of other folk.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"postaviti za nasljednika, učiniti nasljednicima","en":"to appoint as successor, to make successors"},"passage":["وَرَبُّكَ","ٱلْغَنِىُّ","ذُو","ٱلرَّحْمَةِ","إِن","يَشَأْ","يُذْهِبْكُمْ","وَيَسْتَخْلِفْ","مِنۢ","بَعْدِكُم","مَّا","يَشَآءُ","كَمَآ","أَنشَأَكُم","مِّن","ذُرِّيَّةِ","قَوْمٍ","ءَاخَرِينَ"],"marked":[7],"facts":{"verb":"اسْتَخْلَفَ"}},{"id":"istakhlafa-7-129-16","words":["verb:istakhlafa"],"options":[{"bs":"i postavlja vas za nasljednike","en":"and he/it appoints you (all) as successors"},{"bs":"i postavlja za nasljednika","en":"and he/it appoints as successor"},{"bs":"zaista će ih postaviti za nasljednike","en":"surely he/it will appoint them as successors"},{"bs":"postavio je za nasljednika","en":"he/it appointed as successor"}],"ref":"7:129","answerWord":"وَيَسْتَخْلِفَكُمْ","answerSound":"audio/9895c9cae4ce32bb2bf2.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"They said: We suffered hurt before thou camest unto us, and since thou hast come unto us. He said: It may be that your Lord is going to destroy your adversary and make you viceroys in the earth, that He may see how ye behave.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"postaviti za nasljednika, učiniti nasljednicima","en":"to appoint as successor, to make successors"},"passage":["قَالُوٓا۟","أُوذِينَا","مِن","قَبْلِ","أَن","تَأْتِيَنَا","وَمِنۢ","بَعْدِ","مَا","جِئْتَنَا","قَالَ","عَسَىٰ","رَبُّكُمْ","أَن","يُهْلِكَ","عَدُوَّكُمْ","وَيَسْتَخْلِفَكُمْ","فِى","ٱلْأَرْضِ","فَيَنظُرَ","كَيْفَ","تَعْمَلُونَ"],"marked":[16],"facts":{"verb":"اسْتَخْلَفَ"}},{"id":"istakhlafa-11-57-8","words":["verb:istakhlafa"],"options":[{"bs":"i postavlja za nasljednika","en":"and he/it appoints as successor"},{"bs":"zaista će ih postaviti za nasljednike","en":"surely he/it will appoint them as successors"},{"bs":"postavio je za nasljednika","en":"he/it appointed as successor"},{"bs":"i postavlja vas za nasljednike","en":"and he/it appoints you (all) as successors"}],"ref":"11:57","answerWord":"وَيَسْتَخْلِفُ","answerSound":"audio/1842650b0fb78f20db3b.m4a","quranTranslation":{"text":"And if ye turn away, still I have conveyed unto you that wherewith I was sent unto you, and my Lord will set in place of you a folk other than you. Ye cannot injure Him at all. Lo! my Lord is Guardian over all things.","by":"M. M. Pickthall (1930), via tanzil.net"},"gloss":{"bs":"postaviti za nasljednika, učiniti nasljednicima","en":"to appoint as successor, to make successors"},"passage":["فَإِن","تَوَلَّوْا۟","فَقَدْ","أَبْلَغْتُكُم","مَّآ","أُرْسِلْتُ","بِهِۦٓ","إِلَيْكُمْ","وَيَسْتَخْلِفُ","رَبِّى","قَوْمًا","غَيْرَكُمْ","وَلَا","تَضُرُّونَهُۥ","شَيْـًٔا","إِنَّ","رَبِّى","عَلَىٰ","كُلِّ","شَىْءٍ","حَفِيظٌ"],"marked":[8],"facts":{"verb":"اسْتَخْلَفَ"}}]